=== D47: spoken_video_content v2 applies D33; youtube v3 ===
$ spoken_policy
  spoken_video_content v2: collect=True ai=True retention=30
   - Public videos only, and only videos linked to a catalogue project
   - Captions first (youtube-transcript-api); audio through yt-dlp only when no usable caption track exists (D33)
   - No sign-in, cookies, proxies or bot-check workarounds; a refusal or a bot check stops the attempt and is recorded
   - Audio is deleted after transcription; it is never stored, shared or republished
   - Transcripts keep the original timing and language; translations are stored separately
   - Speech is attributed to the video with the speaker unknown unless the platform states it; comments stay separate
